<title>PORTUGAL: Maastricht terms only yardstick for euro - Portugal.</title>
<headline>Maastricht terms only yardstick for euro - Portugal.</headline>
<dateline>LISBON 1997-02-05</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Maastricht criteria are the only yardsticks for deciding which countries join the first wave of Economic and Monetary Union, Prime Minister Antonio Guterres said.</p>
<p>&quot;Portugal will not accept any other interpretation than the Maastricht Treaty,&quot; Guterres said, responding to concerns that political factors could outweigh economic accomplishments in deciding which states join EMU from the outset in 1999.</p>
<p>&quot;Portugal is on the right track to join the single currency and meet the convergence criteria,&quot; he told reporters.</p>
<p>&quot;We want to be admitted on our own merits. We are not part of any bloc and we don't want to be evaluated in conjunction with any others,&quot; he said.</p>
<p>-- Lisbon newsroom +351-1-3538254</p>
</text>
